Spec folder: specs/cli-external-orchestration/082-opencode-v1-v2-dual-compat/040-dispatch-lint-held-fixes (pre-approved, skip Gate 3)

ROLE: Act as a code agent. Make exactly one change, plus its test.

Problem: in `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-audit.mjs`, `hasDispatchText` (around line 282) decides whether an expanded token such as `"$(codex exec task)"` holds a dispatch. Its Codex line requires a `-p`/`--print` flag after `codex exec`, but Codex has no print flag: `directExecutor` and the `DISPATCH_SHAPES` entry both treat `codex exec` alone as the dispatch. So `inspectDispatch('echo "$(codex exec task)"')` returns `{ kind: 'none' }`, and the Pi preflight, which returns early on `none`, lets that Codex run skip authorization and every hard rule.

Fix: change only the Codex line in `hasDispatchText` to match `codex exec` without a print flag, the same shape `DISPATCH_SHAPES` uses (`/\bcodex\s+exec\b/`). Change no other line of the function and no other function.

Test: in `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-audit.test.mjs`, add rows to the existing `it.each` table in `describe('inspectDispatch', ...)`, next to the `quoted command substitution` row:
- `['quoted codex substitution', 'echo "$(codex exec task)"', { kind: 'ambiguous' }]`
- `['codex substitution', '$(codex exec task)', { kind: 'ambiguous' }]`
- `['backtick codex substitution', 'echo "`codex exec task`"', { kind: 'ambiguous' }]` (write the backticks so the string literal is valid JavaScript)
Keep every existing row unchanged.

Comments keep the durable WHY and never name spec paths, phases, or task, review or finding ids.

